insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('8e4ac44e-31df-5b64-bab0-273cce3a0312', 'wg8-writing-with-evidence-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Draft: Why the Otters Returned$q$, $q$(1) In the article "Otters Come Home," Lena Marsh describes how river otters returned to the Alder River after forty years away. (2) Otters are some of the most playful animals anyone could hope to see. (3) Marsh explains that a paper mill once poured waste into the river, and the small fish that otters eat almost vanished. (4) After the town passed new water rules in 2009, the fish slowly began to return. (5) Marsh reports that "by 2018, volunteers counted otter tracks along six miles of riverbank." (6) This timeline shows that the otters came back only after their food supply recovered.

(7) ____, Marsh describes how students from Alder Middle School planted willow trees along the banks. (8) The roots held the soil in place, so less mud washed into the water. (9) Marsh adds that otters later dug dens among those same roots. (10) This detail shows that people helped the otters by repairing their habitat, not just by cleaning the water.

(11) The otters are back, and the river is a nice place to visit now.$q$, 'draft')
