   $q$Which revision of sentence 11 best concludes the draft while staying true to the evidence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Overall, Fofanah shows that Mr. Saleh was the most important painter in the whole project.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Fofanah's details, from the busier tunnel to Mr. Saleh's new friendships, show that the mural helped neighbors connect.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Overall, Fofanah shows that the city should pay to paint murals in every tunnel it owns.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-recommendation"},{"text":"Overall, the walkers counted in the spring prove that the Saturday market made money.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Fofanah's details, from the busier tunnel to Mr. Saleh's new friendships, show that the mural helped neighbors connect.$q$, $q$The best conclusion gathers evidence from both paragraphs and restates the analysis about connection. The article reports on one mural, so saying the city should paint every tunnel is a recommendation the evidence does not support.$q$, 'draft', '0c42a82c-b490-5e05-a750-5b0850d2b59a')
