   $q$How does sentence 3 support the claim in sentence 2?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It proves that the phone rule was a failure that the school regretted.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-evidence"},{"text":"It supports the part of the claim saying many students disliked the rule at first.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that students made new friends during lunch that month.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-evidence"},{"text":"It shows that lunch monitors saw more students playing board games.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misattributes-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It supports the part of the claim saying many students disliked the rule at first.$q$, $q$The claim says students disliked the rule at first, and a petition with more than two hundred names shows that dislike. The petition does not prove the rule failed, since later sentences show students talking more.$q$, 'draft', 'a9580e23-ac5e-5950-87da-7296db5e38be')
