  ('505d559b-f9b7-513e-b559-bb58194ea0d9', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which revision of sentence 11 best concludes the draft while staying true to the evidence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"That is why sixty percent of the students made a new friend at lunch.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-single-detail"},{"text":"Abara's evidence suggests that a phone-free lunch, though unpopular at first, gave students more chances to connect.","is_correct":true},{"text":"That is why every school should ban phones in every class and every hallway.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"That is why the students who signed the petition were wrong to complain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-judgment"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Abara's evidence suggests that a phone-free lunch, though unpopular at first, gave students more chances to connect.$q$, $q$The choice about a phone-free lunch giving students more chances to connect sums up both parts of the claim, the early dislike and the new connections, without going beyond the article. The article studied only lunch at one school, so banning phones in every class overstates the evidence.$q$, 'draft', 'a9580e23-ac5e-5950-87da-7296db5e38be')
