  ('52222888-205c-5507-a10a-b189a01d341e', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g8-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which claim best fills blank 2?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Park's article has seven paragraphs, one photo and a short list of sources.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"structure-not-claim"},{"text":"Bees are insects with six legs, four wings and two antennae on their heads.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Park argues that these solitary bees are gentle, hard-working pollinators that people can easily help.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Park argues that honeybees are the most important insects living on Earth.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-source"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Park argues that these solitary bees are gentle, hard-working pollinators that people can easily help.$q$, $q$The draft goes on to show that solitary bees rarely sting, pollinate well and can be helped with a bee hotel, so the claim about gentle, hard-working pollinators previews all of it. The draft praises mason bees over honeybees, so a claim about honeybees being most important does not fit.$q$, 'draft', '362be4b9-3af6-5c86-8e57-b3f540a62e51')
