   $q$Which revision of sentence 10 best connects it to the claim in sentence 7?$q$, $q$[{"text":"One student, Lupe Ortega, told Moana that her favorite part was the bright color of the bus.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"One student, Lupe Ortega, told Moana she plans to study weather, which is a popular subject.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-irrelevant-comment"},{"text":"One student, Lupe Ortega, told Moana that using the bus's weather station made her decide to study weather.","is_correct":true},{"text":"One student, Lupe Ortega, told Moana she has always wanted to study weather since she was small.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"undercuts-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$One student, Lupe Ortega, told Moana that using the bus's weather station made her decide to study weather.$q$, $q$Sentence 7 says the lab changed students' plans, and the choice about using the bus's weather station shows it caused Lupe's new plan. Saying she "always wanted" to study weather means the bus did not change anything, which weakens the claim.$q$, 'draft', 'f10969c8-3da3-54c7-a142-f56f2f62264c')
